// =============================================================================
// NextScan Studio - the reference the assistant reads about Word's API
// Plan ref: docs/DOCUMENT_WORKSPACE.md
//
// The assistant can change anything in a Word document, because edit_document
// runs a script for the editor's own document API. What stops a model from doing
// it well is not the power but the memory: it half remembers a dozen APIs, and
// this one's names, units and quirks (a paragraph's AddHyperlink replaces its
// text; sizes are half-points; a section break settles what came BEFORE it) are
// its own. So it asks: word_api gives it, on request, the recipes below -- each
// one tried in the running editor -- and the method list of any class, taken from
// the editor itself (GENERATED from it: do not edit the lists by hand; the recipes
// are recipes.txt of the same run).
// =============================================================================
